                            15 *-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
                            16 *  Definition of Compiler Assignable Memory
                            17 *-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
                            18 
                            19 *Volatile marker assignment
                            20 * --- M1000...M1089 reserved for standard M-functions (M00 - M89)
                            21 * --- M1200...M1299 reserved for package device PLC (BLUM, RENISHAW, etc.)
                            22 * --- M1300...M1999 reserved for additional M-functions (M300 - M999)
                            23 * --- M2000...M2799 reserved for EUMACH
                            24 * --- M2800...M2989 reserved for additional PLC error messages (error 800 - 989)
                            25 * --- M4000...M4999 reserved for NC/PLC interface
                            26 * --- M4800...M4999 reserved for standard PLC error messages (error 0 - 200)
                            27 * --- M5000...M5999 reserved for NC/PLC interface
                            28 
                            29 *Non-volatile marker assignment
                            30 * --- M0...M39 reserved for original BASIC program
                            31 * --- M40...M99 reserved for EUMACH
                            32 
                            33 #define /mn   7000 9999              *Marker volatile     max. 1000 - 9999
                            34 #define /mr   200  999               *Marker non volatile max.    0 -  999 (1)
                            35 
                            36 *Volatile byte/word/double-word assignment
                            37 * --- B256...B2047 reserved for NC/PLC interface
                            38 * --- B2048...B2299 reserved for original BASIC program
                            39 * --- B3000...B3199 reserved for EUMACH
                            40 
                            41 *Non-volatile byte/word/double-word assignment
                            42 * --- B0...B39 reserved for original BASIC program
                            43 * --- B40...B55 reserved for EUMACH
                            44 
                            45 #define /bn   6000 9999              *Byte volatile       max. 2048 - 9999
                            46 #define /br   56   255               *Byte non volatile   max.    0 -  255 (1)
                            47 
                            48 * Legend:
                            49 *   (1) - can be modified in oem.cfg
                            50 
                            51 *-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
                            52 *  Definition of Global Symbols
                            53 *-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
                            54 
