                           423 
                           424 *;EUMACH M4x/M6x
                           425 *;       When a clamping axis is active, if emergency stop button is pressed or the guard is open,
                           426 *;       the clamping/unclamping status will return to the power-on status.
                           427 *;       Example:
                           428 *;          Power-on C-axis unclamping -> M64 -> C-axis clamped -> EMG/guard open -> EMG released/guard
                           429 *;          closed -> C-axis unclamping (would prefer C-axis to remain clamped)
                           430 *;       When a clamping axis is controlled by using X150/X151 (such as TVMC area II C rotary axis),
                           431 *;       if this axis is disabled by X150/X151, BG_step_axes[X] will always stay in case 0 due to
                           432 *;       WG_release_axes_X150_X151 = 0.  For the original PLC, WG_activate_control_loop_open will be
                           433 *;       overwritten to power-on status which will cause the following problem.
                           434 *;       1. Power-on rotary axis clamping mode = off -> M64/M65/M66 -> rotary axis clamps for a while
                           435 *;          and then it unclamps again.
                           436 *;       2. Power-on rotary axis clamping mode = on -> M44/M45/M46 -> rotary axis unclamps for a while
                           437 *;          and then it clamps again.
                           438 *;       When PLC modifications marked with "*;EUMACH M4x/M6x" are added (also in INITIAL.SRC), all the
                           439 *;       above problems will be solved.
010E23 81 FD 18 02 00 00   440
       7F 08 81 FD 09 DB 
       FF FF 7D 0A B8 00 
       21 B8 01 0C 38 FF 
       56 34             
