                             3 *-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
                             4 *  Module Description
                             5 *
                             6 *    - Four soft keys have been added to integrate the IPC.
                             7 *         - Soft_key_IPC_active
                             8 *         - Soft_key_override_S_IPC
                             9 *         - Soft_key_override_FMAX_IPC
                            10 *         - Soft_key_override_F_IPC
                            11 *      In addition to <Soft_key_IPC_active> the IPC features a key which
                            12 *      also serves to switch the IPC on and off.
                            13 *    - On TNC side the IPC can be deactivated by key <Home>.
                            14 *    - The overrides are connected to the analog inputs 1/2 X48 the MC 42x
                            15 *      via a separate cable. An additional averaging function with
                            16 *      hysteresis evaluation ensures a continuous characteristic curve.
                            17 *    - When the IPC is active, the switchover to IPC overrides takes
                            18 *      place by pressing the corresponding soft key or by changing the
                            19 *      IPC overrides by more than 10 % (without HSCI).
                            20 *    - On HSCI facilities with MB6xxx exists only one soft key to shift
                            21 *      all IPC overrides. This has to be pressed for activation or
                            22 *      deactivation in general.
                            23 *    - The operation on the TNC side is accordingly after the IP was
                            24 *      deactivated.
                            25 *    - Settings IPC TNCterminal
                            26 *        User: administrator (case sensitive)
                            27 *        password: 807667
                            28 *        IP address: IP Address of the TNC
                            29 *        TNCterminal - ControlPanel\Settings\Edit\PLC Interaction [address]
                            30 *          Connect Marker             -> 'IPC_61x0.src'\ML_IPC_61x0_connect
                            31 *          Disconnect Marker          -> 'IPC_61x0.src'\ML_IPC_61x0_disconnect
                            32 *          Disable Connect Key Marker -> 'IPC_61x0.src'\ML_IPC_61x0_disable
                            33 *          Connect Status Marker      -> 'IPC_61x0.src'\ML_IPC_61x0_connected
                            34 *          Heart Beat Marker          -> 'IPC_61x0.src'\ML_IPC_61x0_clock_monitoring
                            35 *
                            36 *-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
                            37 
     K30                    38 #define /s    KL_factor_voltage_range                  K +30
